1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:02,169
Where are you going?

2
00:00:02,236 --> 00:00:03,270
Huh? Hey!

3
00:00:03,337 --> 00:00:05,687
What are you,
a Joseon Dynasty noble lady?

4
00:00:05,737 --> 00:00:06,940
EPISODE 19

5
00:00:07,007 --> 00:00:08,809
Why make a fuss? Get in here.

6
00:00:08,876 --> 00:00:09,977
Oh! Let go of me!

7
00:00:10,043 --> 00:00:11,512
Let go of me! Let go!

8
00:00:11,578 --> 00:00:13,947
Come on, get inside.

9
00:00:17,851 --> 00:00:19,319
Let go of me!

10
00:00:19,386 --> 00:00:21,889
Come on, get over here.

11
00:00:23,090 --> 00:00:24,525
Hwa-ran.

12
00:00:25,959 --> 00:00:27,427
Ki-jun.

13
00:00:28,562 --> 00:00:31,031
Uh… What are you doing here?

14
00:00:31,698 --> 00:00:32,566
It's just…

15
00:00:32,633 --> 00:00:35,335
You have no business etiquette.
Get in here.

16
00:00:37,337 --> 00:00:39,339
Let go of her hand, you bastard!

17
00:00:39,406 --> 00:00:40,507
Agh!

18
00:00:40,574 --> 00:00:41,608
Ugh.

19
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:45,579
Let go of me.

20
00:00:46,346 --> 00:00:48,115
What on earth are you doing here?

21
00:00:48,181 --> 00:00:49,283
What are you doing?

22
00:00:49,983 --> 00:00:53,921
To pay my mother's hospital bills,
I had no other choice.

23
00:00:53,987 --> 00:00:55,489
So you do a job like this?

24
00:00:55,556 --> 00:00:56,757
Are you crazy?

25
00:00:56,823 --> 00:00:59,126
I don't want to work here either.

26
00:00:59,192 --> 00:01:03,063
But what can I do
when I have nowhere else to work?

27
00:01:04,364 --> 00:01:06,300
It breaks my heart too.

28
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:08,635
It's tearing me apart.

29
00:01:16,877 --> 00:01:18,912
Hey! Who is that?

30
00:01:18,979 --> 00:01:20,047
Hey!

31
00:01:20,847 --> 00:01:22,449
You, get over here.

32
00:01:22,516 --> 00:01:23,984
You're dead meat, you punk!

33
00:01:24,051 --> 00:01:26,353
What, you bastard? What did you say?

34
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:27,921
Sir, calm down. Please stop.

35
00:01:27,988 --> 00:01:29,122
Get out of the way, you bastard!

36
00:01:29,623 --> 00:01:30,490
Crazy bastard!

37
00:01:30,557 --> 00:01:32,059
I'll kill you, bastard!

38
00:01:32,125 --> 00:01:33,293
You little punk!

39
00:01:33,794 --> 00:01:35,963
You're dead meat today! Dead meat!

40
00:01:36,029 --> 00:01:37,965
Stop it. Please stop it.

41
00:01:38,031 --> 00:01:39,933
Do you want to die?

42
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,768
You, get over here.

43
00:01:41,835 --> 00:01:44,705
That bastard! You really want to die?

44
00:01:51,078 --> 00:01:52,579
Break it up. Stop it.

45
00:01:52,646 --> 00:01:55,115
Let me go! I'll kill that bastard!

46
00:01:55,182 --> 00:01:56,116
I said stop it!

47
00:01:56,183 --> 00:01:58,652
That punk hit me like this first!

48
00:01:59,786 --> 00:02:02,189
Let's talk about that at the station.

49
00:02:03,323 --> 00:02:05,492
Looks like you got hit too, miss.

50
00:02:05,559 --> 00:02:07,160
How could you hit a woman?

51
00:02:07,227 --> 00:02:09,096
Are you okay?

52
00:02:09,162 --> 00:02:11,431
You'll have to come with us too, miss.

53
00:02:11,498 --> 00:02:12,566
It's no big deal.

54
00:02:12,633 --> 00:02:14,101
Just go give a statement.

55
00:02:17,871 --> 00:02:19,940
What's with you?

56
00:02:20,007 --> 00:02:21,842
That's suspicious.

57
00:02:21,908 --> 00:02:23,777
Miss, let me see your ID.

58
00:02:28,048 --> 00:02:30,017
Your ID, please.

59
00:02:31,785 --> 00:02:33,086
-Miss, hurry!
-Hey!

60
00:02:33,153 --> 00:02:35,255
-Run!
-Grab her!

61
00:02:38,659 --> 00:02:40,127
Miss!

62
00:02:40,193 --> 00:02:41,395
-No!
-Stop there!

63
00:02:41,461 --> 00:02:42,729
-Hey, grab her!
-Go!

64
00:02:42,796 --> 00:02:44,498
Miss!

65
00:03:08,555 --> 00:03:11,324
-Name?
-Han Ki-jun.

66
00:03:11,391 --> 00:03:13,427
Date of birth.

67
00:03:13,994 --> 00:03:17,798
Um, sir, what happened to the woman
who was with me earlier?

68
00:03:17,864 --> 00:03:19,232
Who?

69
00:03:19,299 --> 00:03:23,136
Oh, the illegal immigrant?
We sent her to the Immigration Office.

70
00:03:23,203 --> 00:03:26,873
The Immigration Office?
Then what happens to her now?

71
00:03:26,940 --> 00:03:30,777
A few days in a detention center,
then she'll probably get deported.

72
00:03:31,478 --> 00:03:33,113
Date of birth.

73
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:43,490
Tell me where the five billion won is!

74
00:03:44,758 --> 00:03:47,928
Keep acting this way?
Shall I call the congressman's office?

75
00:03:47,994 --> 00:03:49,429
All right.

76
00:03:49,496 --> 00:03:51,498
All right.

77
00:03:51,565 --> 00:03:54,367
I'll talk. I'll tell you.

78
00:03:54,434 --> 00:03:56,002
Fine. Where is it?

79
00:03:59,306 --> 00:04:02,576
Uh… since I just woke up from a coma,

80
00:04:02,642 --> 00:04:04,811
I can't quite remember.

81
00:04:07,681 --> 00:04:10,350
I'll sleep now and tell you tomorrow.

82
00:04:11,685 --> 00:04:14,855
Are you kidding me right now?
Aren't you going to talk?

83
00:04:20,594 --> 00:04:24,264
We can't let that jerk run away,
so keep a tight watch on him.

84
00:04:24,331 --> 00:04:27,734
Keep your eyes wide open
and watch him all night, got it?

85
00:04:27,801 --> 00:04:30,504
Sure, don't you worry!

86
00:04:40,947 --> 00:04:42,616
What is this?

87
00:04:49,656 --> 00:04:51,191
Huh? He's gone?

88
00:04:51,258 --> 00:04:53,794
Where did that jerk go?

89
00:04:53,860 --> 00:04:55,595
The jerk bolted.

90
00:04:55,662 --> 00:04:57,964
What are you doing? Get up right now!

91
00:04:58,031 --> 00:05:01,234
I could die of embarrassment, really.

92
00:05:04,037 --> 00:05:06,973
This time, we'll make a caffe latte.

93
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:11,578
For a caffe latte,
first pour in one shot of espresso.

94
00:05:11,645 --> 00:05:14,214
Then, we'll pour steamed milk on top

95
00:05:14,281 --> 00:05:17,484
up to the latte line.

96
00:05:31,865 --> 00:05:34,000
EDIYA COFFEE GRAND OPENING

97
00:05:35,435 --> 00:05:37,470
Keep customers happy on opening day

98
00:05:37,537 --> 00:05:39,005
and wipe every corner well.

99
00:05:39,072 --> 00:05:40,707
Yes, ma'am.

100
00:05:43,443 --> 00:05:45,111
President Hwang!

101
00:05:46,146 --> 00:05:47,380
You all made it!

102
00:05:47,447 --> 00:05:51,384
Wow, it looks impressive all fixed up.

103
00:05:51,451 --> 00:05:54,154
-It sure does.
-Congrats on finally opening!

104
00:05:54,221 --> 00:05:56,089
Thanks, Yun-hui.

105
00:05:56,156 --> 00:05:58,892
It's way prettier and nicer
than our place, dear.

106
00:05:58,959 --> 00:06:00,093
He spent big, huh?

107
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:01,394
Of course I did.

108
00:06:01,461 --> 00:06:04,698
You know I go all out when I spend.

109
00:06:05,498 --> 00:06:08,702
So our I-ji… Wait, no.

110
00:06:08,768 --> 00:06:10,136
You're the boss now.

111
00:06:10,203 --> 00:06:13,440
Shall we try coffee made by the boss?

112
00:06:13,506 --> 00:06:16,243
Now that I've seen I-ji,

113
00:06:16,309 --> 00:06:17,210
may I head out?

114
00:06:17,277 --> 00:06:18,945
Why? Where are you going?

115
00:06:19,012 --> 00:06:21,715
Huh? Um… I have plans.

116
00:06:21,781 --> 00:06:25,018
An old neighbor of ours lives nearby.

117
00:06:25,085 --> 00:06:26,286
I'd like to stop by.

118
00:06:26,353 --> 00:06:28,021
Who? What's their name?

119
00:06:28,088 --> 00:06:29,055
Their name?

120
00:06:29,122 --> 00:06:31,658
In… Um, it's In-ja.

121
00:06:31,725 --> 00:06:34,461
You wouldn't know.
She moved when you were young.

122
00:06:34,527 --> 00:06:36,229
I'll head out now, then.

123
00:06:36,296 --> 00:06:37,497
Good luck, I-ji.

124
00:06:37,564 --> 00:06:39,332
-Have a good day.
-Okay, bye.

125
00:06:39,399 --> 00:06:41,201
-Take care.
-Sure.

126
00:06:42,035 --> 00:06:44,437
In-ja? I've never heard that name.

127
00:06:44,504 --> 00:06:46,740
In-ja, In-ja…

128
00:06:46,806 --> 00:06:50,277
In-ja! No way!

129
00:06:50,343 --> 00:06:52,012
Mom!

130
00:06:54,147 --> 00:06:55,815
I knew this would happen!

131
00:06:55,882 --> 00:06:57,284
Mom!

132
00:06:57,350 --> 00:06:58,551
Mom!

133
00:07:00,253 --> 00:07:03,123
-What should we do?
-We do what we always do.

134
00:07:03,189 --> 00:07:04,824
Run!

135
00:07:06,359 --> 00:07:08,495
Mom, why are you running?

136
00:07:08,561 --> 00:07:10,063
Come back here!

137
00:07:10,130 --> 00:07:11,298
Mom!

138
00:07:13,466 --> 00:07:16,369
Anyway, what are you guys doing
instead of eating?

139
00:07:18,104 --> 00:07:20,473
You can see we're waiting for a call.

140
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:22,275
They should've called by now.

141
00:07:22,342 --> 00:07:25,278
They said they'd call today.
Why haven't they called?

142
00:07:25,345 --> 00:07:28,181
They'll call when it's time.
Just eat, you punks.

143
00:07:31,051 --> 00:07:33,586
-Here it is.
-It's here.

144
00:07:37,724 --> 00:07:39,359
Hello?

145
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:42,729
Yes, yes.

146
00:07:45,665 --> 00:07:47,300
Yes.

147
00:07:49,069 --> 00:07:50,704
Yes.

148
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:57,944
Why did you just say "yes, yes, yes"?
What did they say?

149
00:07:58,011 --> 00:07:59,746
-They said no?
-No.

150
00:07:59,813 --> 00:08:02,882
No, they want to sign us right now.

151
00:08:02,949 --> 00:08:04,884
They said they'll send a car here!

152
00:08:04,951 --> 00:08:07,253
-Hey, hey!
-Don't get so overly excited!

153
00:08:08,421 --> 00:08:11,424
It doesn't feel real.
Hey, this isn't a dream, right?

154
00:08:11,491 --> 00:08:13,259
It's not a dream! At this point,

155
00:08:13,326 --> 00:08:16,296
there's no need to dream!
Our hard times are over now!

156
00:08:17,397 --> 00:08:20,467
Congratulations! That's so wonderful.

157
00:08:21,701 --> 00:08:23,570
-Congratulations.
-Thanks.

158
00:08:23,636 --> 00:08:24,771
We can't waste time.

159
00:08:24,838 --> 00:08:26,039
They're sending a car,

160
00:08:26,106 --> 00:08:28,241
so let's pack fast. You too, Yun-a!

161
00:08:28,308 --> 00:08:30,577
My goodness, everyone's so busy.

162
00:08:33,847 --> 00:08:35,682
My, they sure must be happy.

163
00:08:37,784 --> 00:08:40,186
Just like this, and this.

164
00:08:40,253 --> 00:08:43,723
Anyway, our Excellent Souls
is finally being resurrected!

165
00:08:44,524 --> 00:08:47,761
How is this even possible?
This is an absolute miracle!

166
00:08:47,827 --> 00:08:49,429
You can say that again.

167
00:08:52,132 --> 00:08:54,601
Why the long face? Are you upset?

168
00:08:54,667 --> 00:08:57,904
No, I just feel a bit uneasy…

169
00:08:57,971 --> 00:09:01,374
Uneasy about what? We're all done now.

170
00:09:03,843 --> 00:09:06,279
Hey… what about the cabbages?

171
00:09:06,346 --> 00:09:09,015
Why talk about cabbages
when we're signing a deal?

172
00:09:09,082 --> 00:09:12,685
Dude, we worked so hard to grow them.

173
00:09:12,752 --> 00:09:16,489
Darn it, let's go make sure
the cover is on properly.

174
00:09:16,556 --> 00:09:18,124
That little guy can't freeze.

175
00:09:18,191 --> 00:09:21,394
Jeez, fine, okay.

176
00:09:29,035 --> 00:09:33,506
Do I look crazy enough to share
this precious money with you guys?

177
00:09:33,573 --> 00:09:37,010
Why did they have to pile
these damn cabbages right here?

178
00:09:37,077 --> 00:09:38,545
Why do we have to go there?

179
00:09:38,611 --> 00:09:39,479
They'll freeze.

180
00:09:39,546 --> 00:09:41,948
Hey! What are you doing over there?

181
00:09:42,015 --> 00:09:43,483
-Hey!

182
00:09:43,550 --> 00:09:45,485
Darn it.

183
00:09:47,554 --> 00:09:48,788
Hey!

184
00:09:48,855 --> 00:09:50,490
Darn it, hey!

185
00:09:52,926 --> 00:09:54,561
That jerk's an actual thief.

186
00:09:55,462 --> 00:09:57,530
-Right? How is he so fast?
-Seriously.

187
00:09:57,597 --> 00:09:59,966
Cabbages cost nothing. Why steal them?

188
00:10:00,033 --> 00:10:02,235
Jeez, we really need a plan for this.

189
00:10:02,302 --> 00:10:04,070
What are y'all doing over there?

190
00:10:06,106 --> 00:10:08,141
Hello.

191
00:10:08,208 --> 00:10:09,542
Something the matter?

192
00:10:09,609 --> 00:10:12,579
Some jerk tried to steal our cabbages.

193
00:10:12,645 --> 00:10:15,582
What? Cabbage prices hit rock bottom,

194
00:10:15,648 --> 00:10:17,550
so why steal what's worth pennies?

195
00:10:17,617 --> 00:10:19,419
Tell me about it.

196
00:10:20,019 --> 00:10:22,055
Could we ask a small favor, brother?

197
00:10:22,122 --> 00:10:24,491
We're off to Seoul.
Please watch our cabbages.

198
00:10:24,557 --> 00:10:26,092
Why should I?

199
00:10:26,159 --> 00:10:28,661
I have a second date
over rice wine, you know.

200
00:10:28,728 --> 00:10:33,066
Then we'll get you a bottle of whiskey
on our way back from Seoul. Whiskey!

201
00:10:33,133 --> 00:10:34,000
Safe travels.

202
00:10:34,067 --> 00:10:35,935
Thank you very much.

203
00:10:36,002 --> 00:10:37,070
We're late. Hurry!

204
00:10:37,137 --> 00:10:38,771
Thank you.

205
00:10:43,243 --> 00:10:46,746
You jerk! You bolted
the second I looked away?

206
00:10:46,813 --> 00:10:48,414
He must be somewhere nearby.

207
00:10:48,481 --> 00:10:49,516
I know.

208
00:10:49,582 --> 00:10:51,518
Just try running away…

209
00:10:53,052 --> 00:10:54,354
Ow, that hurts!

210
00:10:56,089 --> 00:10:58,424
-Huh?
-Darn it!

211
00:10:58,491 --> 00:11:00,460
Where are you going, you punk?

212
00:11:00,527 --> 00:11:03,229
Spill it now,
or I'll really tell them this time.

213
00:11:03,296 --> 00:11:06,866
Okay, okay! I'll tell you!

214
00:11:06,933 --> 00:11:08,801
Goodness.

215
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:15,742
Goodbye, Yun-a.

216
00:11:15,808 --> 00:11:18,645
Thank you so much for everything.

217
00:11:18,711 --> 00:11:20,013
Take care too, Min-ho.

218
00:11:20,079 --> 00:11:22,415
Okay, pretty lady! Come visit again.

219
00:11:23,049 --> 00:11:25,285
I will. Goodbye, everyone.

220
00:11:25,351 --> 00:11:27,820
All right, have a safe trip.

221
00:11:27,887 --> 00:11:30,223
-Goodbye.
-Take care.

222
00:11:30,290 --> 00:11:32,592
Let's get going. We'll be back soon!

223
00:11:32,659 --> 00:11:34,460
Okay, travel safe.

224
00:11:34,527 --> 00:11:36,496
Okay, I won't walk you out.

225
00:11:36,563 --> 00:11:40,266
So if they sign the contract,
are those boys going back up too?

226
00:11:40,333 --> 00:11:44,103
For a while, all that noise
made this place really feel alive.

227
00:11:44,170 --> 00:11:45,705
It'll feel so lonely now.

228
00:11:45,772 --> 00:11:47,140
It really will.

229
00:11:47,740 --> 00:11:49,842
Where is it? Is it still far?

230
00:11:49,909 --> 00:11:51,611
Well, where is it?

231
00:11:52,178 --> 00:11:54,747
We're here. It's right here.

232
00:11:54,814 --> 00:11:57,283
What? Right here?

233
00:11:57,850 --> 00:12:00,453
That's those nutcases' yard.

234
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:02,021
Damn it.

235
00:12:02,088 --> 00:12:05,592
With the money right under our noses,
we dug up the wrong places.

236
00:12:06,426 --> 00:12:08,261
So where's the money?

237
00:12:08,328 --> 00:12:11,231
It's under that pile of cabbages.

238
00:12:11,297 --> 00:12:13,099
Under there?

239
00:12:13,166 --> 00:12:16,002
If they were going to stack cabbages,

240
00:12:16,069 --> 00:12:18,204
why stack them there, of all places?

241
00:12:18,271 --> 00:12:22,041
So what? We'll just move the cabbages.

242
00:12:22,642 --> 00:12:24,611
Come on, let's go.

243
00:12:25,478 --> 00:12:29,115
What fancy liquor will they buy?

244
00:12:29,182 --> 00:12:33,386
But I promised her I'd quit drinking.

245
00:12:33,953 --> 00:12:37,423
Anyway, what kind of jerk
would try to steal these cabbages

246
00:12:37,490 --> 00:12:39,525
we worked so hard to grow?

247
00:12:39,592 --> 00:12:41,861
Just try showing up, just try it!

248
00:12:46,599 --> 00:12:48,801
I'm so bored.

249
00:12:54,574 --> 00:12:56,743
Why is that guy straining so hard?

250
00:12:56,809 --> 00:12:58,645
I know. What do we do?

251
00:12:58,711 --> 00:13:01,614
What else can we do?
We have to wait until he leaves.

252
00:13:01,681 --> 00:13:04,884
If you had told us sooner,
this wouldn't have happened.

253
00:13:04,951 --> 00:13:07,086
Why are you taking it out on me?

254
00:13:07,153 --> 00:13:10,223
And why do you keep talking down to me?

255
00:13:10,290 --> 00:13:12,392
You're way too young to act like that.

256
00:13:15,395 --> 00:13:18,197
I… I'm sorry.

257
00:13:18,264 --> 00:13:19,732
It's just because I'm mad.

258
00:13:19,799 --> 00:13:21,968
Why is that guy still not leaving?

259
00:13:22,035 --> 00:13:23,569
It's okay, he's leaving.

260
00:13:23,636 --> 00:13:26,072
I know, goodness…

261
00:13:38,951 --> 00:13:42,055
The contract is signed,
so let's do great work together.

262
00:13:42,121 --> 00:13:44,257
Yes, thank you. Thank you so much.

263
00:13:44,324 --> 00:13:48,161
I will work myself to the bone!

264
00:13:48,227 --> 00:13:51,164
Got it. Come right up
once you wrap up in the country.

265
00:13:51,230 --> 00:13:53,333
Yes, understood. Thank you, thank you.

266
00:13:53,399 --> 00:13:54,934
I said I got it. Go on now.

267
00:13:55,001 --> 00:13:58,338
Min-gi, I'll talk to the CEO first.

268
00:13:58,404 --> 00:14:00,740
Okay, I'll wait in the lobby.

269
00:14:00,807 --> 00:14:03,009
Even the air here is different, sir!

270
00:14:03,076 --> 00:14:05,445
-Thank you.
-I will work hard, sir.

271
00:14:05,511 --> 00:14:07,780
Thank you very much.

272
00:14:07,847 --> 00:14:09,515
Thank you!

273
00:14:15,355 --> 00:14:16,622
-Yes!

274
00:14:16,689 --> 00:14:17,890
Hey, am I dreaming?

275
00:14:17,957 --> 00:14:19,392
We just got kicked out,

276
00:14:19,459 --> 00:14:21,627
and we signed with this company again…

277
00:14:21,694 --> 00:14:23,262
We're finally going to debut.

278
00:14:23,329 --> 00:14:24,397
Our debut!

279
00:14:25,298 --> 00:14:27,133
I'm really getting choked up.

280
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:28,368
Are you that happy?

281
00:14:28,434 --> 00:14:31,003
Of course I am! Aren't you, dude?

282
00:14:31,070 --> 00:14:34,006
But it'd be even better
if Ki-jun were here too.

283
00:14:34,507 --> 00:14:35,708
I know.

284
00:14:37,443 --> 00:14:39,278
Hey, why do you look like that?

285
00:14:39,345 --> 00:14:40,279
You not happy?

286
00:14:40,346 --> 00:14:41,881
Um… I'm happy.

287
00:14:44,016 --> 00:14:47,120
Hey, hey, I need to run
back to the CEO's office.

288
00:14:47,186 --> 00:14:49,188
-I left my phone in there.
-Okay.

289
00:14:49,722 --> 00:14:51,491
Hey, hurry back!

290
00:14:51,557 --> 00:14:53,126
Our photo will hang here too.

291
00:14:53,192 --> 00:14:54,627
Wait, hung up like them?

292
00:14:54,694 --> 00:14:56,429
-Who?
-No, they're no good.

293
00:14:56,496 --> 00:14:57,597
A pic like FTISLAND!

294
00:14:57,663 --> 00:15:00,366
Oh! Am I going to be like Lee Hong-gi?

295
00:15:02,935 --> 00:15:04,370
Since I did as you asked,

296
00:15:04,437 --> 00:15:06,672
now you do whatever I tell you to.

297
00:15:11,077 --> 00:15:14,547
We've suffered massive losses
because of you all this time.

298
00:15:15,148 --> 00:15:17,617
Plus, those punks
clearly won't make a dime,

299
00:15:17,683 --> 00:15:19,852
and I'm even putting out their album,

300
00:15:20,386 --> 00:15:22,855
so you have to work twice as hard.

301
00:15:22,922 --> 00:15:24,590
Isn't that right?

302
00:15:24,657 --> 00:15:26,426
I already said I would.

303
00:15:27,894 --> 00:15:29,595
If you're done, I'll be going.

304
00:15:35,935 --> 00:15:37,570
Hyeok.

305
00:15:38,070 --> 00:15:41,274
I knew something felt off.
So this is what it was.

306
00:15:41,340 --> 00:15:43,576
No way this shameless jerk
would do this.

307
00:15:43,643 --> 00:15:45,211
It's just, um…

308
00:15:52,051 --> 00:15:53,853
What do you think you're doing?

309
00:15:54,854 --> 00:15:56,489
Shut your mouth.

310
00:15:58,191 --> 00:15:59,091
Hyeok, wait.

311
00:15:59,158 --> 00:16:02,495
Hyeok! Wait, Hyeok!

312
00:16:05,364 --> 00:16:07,366
Hyeok, wait, let's just talk…

313
00:16:07,433 --> 00:16:08,868
Let go of me!

314
00:16:10,536 --> 00:16:13,306
Why on earth are you going this far?

315
00:16:13,973 --> 00:16:18,311
Is this because of Min-gi and Yun-hui?

316
00:16:19,145 --> 00:16:21,314
Ha, seriously.

317
00:16:21,848 --> 00:16:24,984
Then or now, you haven't changed a bit.

318
00:16:26,252 --> 00:16:27,353
What do you mean?

319
00:16:27,420 --> 00:16:30,289
Stopping at nothing for your greed.

320
00:16:30,857 --> 00:16:32,492
Just like back then.

321
00:16:43,836 --> 00:16:46,472
The CEO hid fancy liquor for himself,

322
00:16:46,539 --> 00:16:48,574
and I definitely saw him drinking it.

323
00:16:48,641 --> 00:16:52,578
Where did he hide it?

324
00:16:52,645 --> 00:16:54,313
Is it in here?

325
00:16:55,047 --> 00:16:56,282
Not here.

326
00:16:56,349 --> 00:16:58,484
Then is it in here?

327
00:17:08,995 --> 00:17:11,430
Yu-na, what are you doing tonight?

328
00:17:11,497 --> 00:17:13,399
How about we grab a drink?

329
00:17:13,466 --> 00:17:16,269
I'll put out your album as promised.

330
00:17:16,335 --> 00:17:19,171
So let's have a drink, okay?

331
00:17:19,972 --> 00:17:21,274
Please let go of me.

332
00:17:22,241 --> 00:17:24,243
Why are you acting like this now?

333
00:17:24,310 --> 00:17:26,312
Don't you want to release your album?

334
00:17:26,379 --> 00:17:27,580
Let's get a drink.

335
00:17:27,647 --> 00:17:30,516
I'll release your album, okay?

336
00:17:33,886 --> 00:17:34,921
Get your hand off!

337
00:17:34,987 --> 00:17:37,123
What? Why are you there?

338
00:17:37,189 --> 00:17:38,291
Not your business.

339
00:17:38,357 --> 00:17:40,359
Yu-na, get out of here!

340
00:17:40,426 --> 00:17:42,528
This bastard's dead, damn it!

341
00:17:44,564 --> 00:17:46,399
Min-gi!

342
00:17:46,465 --> 00:17:48,100
Min-gi!

343
00:17:57,410 --> 00:17:58,811
Han-cheol!

344
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:04,951
The CEO?

345
00:18:17,063 --> 00:18:21,467
Even when we got kicked out over that,
you didn't say a single word.

346
00:18:21,534 --> 00:18:25,204
After what that jerk did to you,
you even put out an album under him.

347
00:18:26,105 --> 00:18:29,542
You were always the type
to do anything for your own greed.

348
00:18:29,609 --> 00:18:31,510
Isn't that right?

349
00:18:31,577 --> 00:18:34,714
I don't want to piggyback on you
like this for an album,

350
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:36,682
not in the slightest.

351
00:18:36,749 --> 00:18:38,517
Min-gi would feel the same way.

352
00:18:39,185 --> 00:18:40,953
-Um, Hyeok.
-What?

353
00:18:41,020 --> 00:18:43,089
Keep it a secret from Min-gi again?

354
00:18:44,957 --> 00:18:47,560
What are you talking about?

355
00:18:49,028 --> 00:18:51,364
Min-gi.

356
00:18:55,768 --> 00:18:58,204
A contract riding Yu-na's coattails?

357
00:18:59,305 --> 00:19:02,375
And what did the CEO do to you?

358
00:19:03,142 --> 00:19:04,777
Tell me.

359
00:19:05,678 --> 00:19:07,913
Is everything I heard true?

360
00:19:10,516 --> 00:19:12,218
You tell me.

361
00:19:12,918 --> 00:19:14,887
I asked if it's all true!

362
00:19:18,057 --> 00:19:19,625
Then why didn't you tell me?

363
00:19:19,692 --> 00:19:22,461
After I humiliated you,
why didn't you tell me? Why!

364
00:19:22,528 --> 00:19:24,530
I'm the one who asked him

365
00:19:24,597 --> 00:19:25,631
to keep it secret.

366
00:19:25,698 --> 00:19:27,600
What?

367
00:19:28,300 --> 00:19:29,935
Why?

368
00:19:30,536 --> 00:19:31,570
Why on earth?

369
00:19:31,637 --> 00:19:34,407
If that got out,
I worried I'd get kicked out too.

370
00:19:34,473 --> 00:19:36,308
I did it because I was scared.

371
00:19:36,842 --> 00:19:40,179
I'm sorry, Min-gi. I'm so sorry.

372
00:19:40,846 --> 00:19:43,649
That bastard.

373
00:19:43,716 --> 00:19:45,985
Hey, Min-gi! Min-gi!

374
00:19:48,521 --> 00:19:50,289
Have the car ready. I'm leaving.

375
00:19:51,791 --> 00:19:53,459
What is this?

376
00:19:54,994 --> 00:19:56,529
Get over here.

377
00:19:57,396 --> 00:19:59,265
Who are you? Are you crazy?

378
00:19:59,331 --> 00:20:01,400
I'm going to kill you today!

379
00:20:01,467 --> 00:20:03,602
-Min-gi!
-Stop!

380
00:20:03,669 --> 00:20:05,838
-Let go!
-Let go of me, seriously!

381
00:20:06,539 --> 00:20:07,606
Let me go!

382
00:20:07,673 --> 00:20:09,842
You heard what that bastard
did to Yu-na!

383
00:20:09,909 --> 00:20:11,477
I'll kill that bastard today!

384
00:20:11,544 --> 00:20:12,578
Hey, let go!

385
00:20:12,645 --> 00:20:14,313
So you knew about it?

386
00:20:14,380 --> 00:20:16,482
You two misunderstood. Misunderstood!

387
00:20:16,549 --> 00:20:18,818
Misunderstood? Stop spouting nonsense.

388
00:20:20,152 --> 00:20:22,488
I wasn't the one who approached Yu-na.

389
00:20:22,555 --> 00:20:25,491
Yu-na, this little bitch,
made me an offer first.

390
00:20:28,494 --> 00:20:29,995
What nonsense is that now?

391
00:20:30,062 --> 00:20:31,497
She asked me to debut her,

392
00:20:31,564 --> 00:20:32,965
saying she'd do anything.

393
00:20:33,032 --> 00:20:35,301
You approached me first, didn't you?

394
00:20:35,367 --> 00:20:36,602
Am I wrong?

395
00:20:37,837 --> 00:20:41,040
After that happened,
you even came and blackmailed me.

396
00:20:41,107 --> 00:20:44,543
You said you'd keep the guys quiet
if I debuted you.

397
00:20:44,610 --> 00:20:45,745
Isn't that right?

398
00:20:49,949 --> 00:20:51,584
Yu-na.

399
00:20:52,518 --> 00:20:55,521
That's all a lie, isn't it? Right?

400
00:21:04,363 --> 00:21:06,499
How could you do this to me?

401
00:21:07,767 --> 00:21:09,401
How could you do this to me?

402
00:21:09,468 --> 00:21:11,137
How could you!

403
00:21:12,104 --> 00:21:13,873
I'm sorry.

404
00:21:13,939 --> 00:21:15,107
I'm so sorry.

405
00:21:33,125 --> 00:21:34,794
It's so cold.

406
00:21:39,231 --> 00:21:42,134
Min-ho, what are you doing here?

407
00:21:42,201 --> 00:21:43,602
Nothing.

408
00:21:47,873 --> 00:21:49,975
Why do you look so down?

409
00:21:50,643 --> 00:21:52,978
Mom… can't you tell him

410
00:21:53,045 --> 00:21:54,947
not to go to Seoul?

411
00:21:55,014 --> 00:21:56,582
Huh?

412
00:21:56,649 --> 00:21:59,552
I don't want Min-gi to go to Seoul.

413
00:22:00,252 --> 00:22:02,822
You tell him not to go.

414
00:22:02,888 --> 00:22:04,056
Please?

415
00:22:04,123 --> 00:22:06,258
How can I do that?

416
00:22:06,325 --> 00:22:09,962
Things worked out for the guys,
so let's send them off happily.

417
00:22:10,029 --> 00:22:12,331
And they said they'd visit often,

418
00:22:12,398 --> 00:22:15,067
so don't be too disappointed.

419
00:22:47,700 --> 00:22:50,636
SEOUL IMMIGRATION OFFICE

420
00:23:12,892 --> 00:23:14,627
Song Hwa-ran.

421
00:23:14,693 --> 00:23:17,029
You have a visitor.

422
00:23:22,668 --> 00:23:24,169
Ki-jun.

423
00:23:31,477 --> 00:23:34,413
What are you doing here…

424
00:23:37,116 --> 00:23:40,953
Hwa-ran, are you all right?

425
00:23:42,388 --> 00:23:44,323
Are you hurt anywhere?

426
00:23:44,390 --> 00:23:46,125
I am fine.

427
00:23:46,792 --> 00:23:48,093
Please don't worry.

428
00:23:49,962 --> 00:23:53,732
I'm sorry, Hwa-ran. It's all my fault.

429
00:23:56,268 --> 00:23:58,237
Please do not say that.

430
00:23:58,304 --> 00:24:00,572
It is not your fault.

431
00:24:00,639 --> 00:24:05,277
I could see you again, even like that,

432
00:24:05,344 --> 00:24:07,346
and I was so relieved.

433
00:24:08,881 --> 00:24:12,818
I couldn't even say goodbye,
and it weighed heavily on my mind.

434
00:24:14,353 --> 00:24:16,488
Ki-jun.

435
00:24:17,523 --> 00:24:20,960
Thank you so much.

436
00:24:22,027 --> 00:24:26,098
After coming here,
I was so lonely and had a hard time.

437
00:24:28,200 --> 00:24:31,804
But I was happy thanks to you.

438
00:24:38,043 --> 00:24:40,512
The memories I shared with you…

439
00:24:41,847 --> 00:24:44,316
I will never forget them
as long as I live.

440
00:24:48,554 --> 00:24:52,224
But why are you in Seoul?
What about the farmwork?

441
00:24:56,462 --> 00:24:58,464
I gave up

442
00:24:58,530 --> 00:25:02,634
on the cabbage farming and the album.

443
00:25:03,802 --> 00:25:06,205
I'm going to face reality now.

444
00:25:06,271 --> 00:25:08,774
A dream is just…

445
00:25:10,209 --> 00:25:13,879
a dream. I finally realized that.

446
00:25:13,946 --> 00:25:15,848
What kind of talk is that?

447
00:25:15,914 --> 00:25:19,418
Once a man starts something,
shouldn't he see it through?

448
00:25:20,386 --> 00:25:21,987
I had no choice.

449
00:25:22,054 --> 00:25:24,056
You had no choice?

450
00:25:24,123 --> 00:25:26,592
That is an excuse, and it is cowardly.

451
00:25:29,461 --> 00:25:33,766
Right, that's all I amount to anyway.

452
00:25:33,832 --> 00:25:37,036
I didn't take you for a total coward.

453
00:25:37,102 --> 00:25:39,638
You came this far to act like this?

454
00:25:39,705 --> 00:25:42,875
The Ki-jun I know isn't like this.

455
00:25:42,941 --> 00:25:44,810
You were immature, reckless,

456
00:25:44,877 --> 00:25:47,546
had no plan, always talked big,

457
00:25:47,613 --> 00:25:49,081
never lost heart in defeat.

458
00:25:49,148 --> 00:25:51,183
That's the kind of person you were.

459
00:25:52,885 --> 00:25:54,319
Hwa-ran…

460
00:25:55,087 --> 00:25:57,256
I'm disappointed in you.

461
00:25:57,322 --> 00:25:59,658
I hate seeing you like this, so leave.

462
00:25:59,725 --> 00:26:01,627
Wait, wait, please wait.

463
00:26:01,693 --> 00:26:04,396
I still have something to say. Wait.

464
00:26:04,463 --> 00:26:05,664
Just a moment.

465
00:26:09,568 --> 00:26:13,072
I'm sorry for acting so pathetic.

466
00:26:14,006 --> 00:26:15,641
All right.

467
00:26:16,241 --> 00:26:18,577
You won't give up, right?

468
00:26:21,480 --> 00:26:23,015
Okay, fine.

469
00:26:23,082 --> 00:26:25,384
I just won't give up, okay? I won't.

470
00:26:26,018 --> 00:26:28,620
Now you sound more like yourself.

471
00:26:28,687 --> 00:26:31,457
Anyway, what did you want to say?

472
00:26:34,093 --> 00:26:36,095
Um…

473
00:26:37,763 --> 00:26:39,731
I mean, well…

474
00:26:40,399 --> 00:26:43,435
What is it? Why beat around the bush?

475
00:26:47,906 --> 00:26:49,074
I love you.

476
00:26:49,141 --> 00:26:52,010
I love you, Hwa-ran.

477
00:26:52,711 --> 00:26:55,080
I really wanted to tell you that.

478
00:26:56,982 --> 00:26:59,017
And…

479
00:26:59,084 --> 00:27:02,721
I swear I'll succeed and come for you.

480
00:27:02,788 --> 00:27:04,957
So don't forget me, and wait for me.

481
00:27:05,023 --> 00:27:06,658
All right?

482
00:27:14,199 --> 00:27:15,400
Visiting time is up.

483
00:27:15,467 --> 00:27:16,869
Please stand up.

484
00:27:16,935 --> 00:27:19,004
Yes.

485
00:27:24,443 --> 00:27:26,111
Okay.

486
00:27:30,482 --> 00:27:32,451
I will be going now.

487
00:27:53,639 --> 00:27:54,840
Hwa-ran, Hwa-ran!

488
00:27:54,907 --> 00:27:58,610
You can't forget me.
You really can't forget me!

489
00:27:58,677 --> 00:28:02,181
I'll definitely come for you,
so don't forget me. Wait for me.

490
00:28:02,748 --> 00:28:05,584
Don't look at other guys. Wait for me.

491
00:28:35,948 --> 00:28:37,816
I'm sorry.

492
00:28:37,883 --> 00:28:39,017
For what?

493
00:28:39,084 --> 00:28:41,653
Sorry I misunderstood you for so long.

494
00:28:43,088 --> 00:28:44,022
I apologize.

495
00:28:44,089 --> 00:28:47,292
Forget it. It's all in the past.

496
00:28:47,359 --> 00:28:49,461
What about you? Are you okay?

497
00:28:53,398 --> 00:28:56,268
Anyway, what do we do now?

498
00:28:56,335 --> 00:28:59,805
The contract's totally down the drain.

499
00:29:02,140 --> 00:29:06,311
Guys, let's call it quits now.

500
00:29:07,045 --> 00:29:07,913
What?

501
00:29:07,980 --> 00:29:13,185
I'm so sick of cabbages and music now.

502
00:29:15,153 --> 00:29:16,588
Let's just give up.

503
00:29:16,655 --> 00:29:19,825
Give up? Don't count us out,
we only count heads of cabbage!

504
00:29:19,891 --> 00:29:21,526
Ki-jun!

505
00:29:21,593 --> 00:29:23,395
Why the shock? Never seen my face?

506
00:29:23,462 --> 00:29:24,329
Why are you here?

507
00:29:24,396 --> 00:29:27,733
Why else? I came to sell cabbages
and release our album.

508
00:29:27,799 --> 00:29:29,101
What?

509
00:29:29,167 --> 00:29:31,670
It's all over. Cabbage prices crashed.

510
00:29:31,737 --> 00:29:34,206
The album deal is dead in the water.

511
00:29:34,273 --> 00:29:36,908
There's just nothing we can do now.

512
00:29:36,975 --> 00:29:39,011
Who says there's nothing we can do?

513
00:29:39,077 --> 00:29:41,580
I heard that's just a cowardly excuse.

514
00:29:41,647 --> 00:29:44,416
What are you saying,
showing up out of nowhere now?

515
00:29:44,483 --> 00:29:45,484
You said you quit?

516
00:29:45,550 --> 00:29:47,085
I was going to quit music.

517
00:29:47,152 --> 00:29:48,620
But come to think of it,

518
00:29:48,687 --> 00:29:51,189
nothing's as fun as
making music with you guys.

519
00:29:52,291 --> 00:29:54,793
And cheer up, guys! What is this?

520
00:29:54,860 --> 00:29:57,262
We still have 100,000 cabbages, right?

521
00:29:57,329 --> 00:29:59,364
We can't do anything without a way.

522
00:29:59,431 --> 00:30:01,933
We can find a way step by step--

523
00:30:02,000 --> 00:30:03,902
Um, I…

524
00:30:03,969 --> 00:30:06,738
Oh, Ki-jun! My goodness!

525
00:30:06,805 --> 00:30:08,573
Hi there! I'm back again.

526
00:30:08,640 --> 00:30:09,775
I'll be back!

527
00:30:09,841 --> 00:30:11,943
You little goblin, popping in and out!

528
00:30:12,010 --> 00:30:14,046
No goodbye, and when'd you get back?

529
00:30:14,112 --> 00:30:16,548
I'm sorry. I had some things going on.

530
00:30:16,615 --> 00:30:19,318
Anyway, I'm glad you're back.

531
00:30:19,384 --> 00:30:21,420
My goodness.

532
00:30:23,188 --> 00:30:26,191
I have something to tell you guys.

533
00:30:26,258 --> 00:30:28,527
Come talk with me.

534
00:30:28,593 --> 00:30:31,596
SALTED CABBAGE BUSINESS PLAN

535
00:30:32,230 --> 00:30:34,266
Salted cabbage business? What's this?

536
00:30:34,333 --> 00:30:37,536
Before making kimchi, you soak
the cabbages in salt water.

537
00:30:37,602 --> 00:30:39,271
You guys all know that, right?

538
00:30:39,971 --> 00:30:41,139
No.

539
00:30:41,206 --> 00:30:44,943
Cabbage soaked in salt water
is called salted cabbage.

540
00:30:45,844 --> 00:30:47,479
And?

541
00:30:48,180 --> 00:30:50,082
Cabbage prices have crashed,

542
00:30:50,148 --> 00:30:52,818
but salted cabbage prices
aren't that bad.

543
00:30:52,884 --> 00:30:56,221
And demand is steadily growing, too.

544
00:30:56,288 --> 00:30:58,557
What do you think? Sounds good, right?

545
00:30:58,623 --> 00:31:00,258
Want to give it a try?

546
00:31:01,660 --> 00:31:04,429
How can we do that
when we don't know anything?

547
00:31:05,030 --> 00:31:06,498
Don't we need to hire help

548
00:31:06,565 --> 00:31:07,933
and have an online store?

549
00:31:07,999 --> 00:31:10,168
I talked to the villagers about it,

550
00:31:10,235 --> 00:31:13,672
and seeing your situation,
they said they'd gladly help.

551
00:31:13,739 --> 00:31:15,173
And the government runs

552
00:31:15,240 --> 00:31:16,541
a free website too!

553
00:31:16,608 --> 00:31:18,643
You could just sell them on there.

554
00:31:18,710 --> 00:31:20,645
What do you say?

555
00:31:20,712 --> 00:31:23,081
Feeling a little tempted, Min-gi?

556
00:31:23,949 --> 00:31:25,784
But is that really possible?

557
00:31:25,851 --> 00:31:28,653
You have to try it first
to know if it's possible!

558
00:31:28,720 --> 00:31:31,022
How else will you put out your album?

559
00:31:31,690 --> 00:31:33,892
Are you giving up here like morons?

560
00:31:33,959 --> 00:31:36,528
Or go all out to the end like real men?

561
00:31:39,931 --> 00:31:42,534
Fine, let's try!
It's unfair to end it like this.

562
00:31:43,535 --> 00:31:47,472
Right, we've come this far.
There's nothing we can't do.

563
00:31:47,539 --> 00:31:48,473
Let's go for it.

564
00:31:48,540 --> 00:31:50,876
Right, we have nothing better to do.

565
00:31:50,942 --> 00:31:52,811
Let's give it a shot, Min-gi.

566
00:31:56,081 --> 00:31:57,983
Hey, you cowardly bastard!

567
00:31:58,049 --> 00:31:59,985
You talked us into coming down here!

568
00:32:00,051 --> 00:32:01,753
So take some responsibility!

569
00:32:01,820 --> 00:32:04,022
You irresponsible bastard! Damn it!

570
00:32:04,089 --> 00:32:05,857
All right, man.

571
00:32:05,924 --> 00:32:11,530
Sink or swim, let's see it to the end.

572
00:32:11,596 --> 00:32:12,697
That's the spirit!

573
00:32:12,764 --> 00:32:14,900
You boys sure have plenty of guts.

574
00:32:14,966 --> 00:32:16,501
You've really got guts.

575
00:32:16,568 --> 00:32:18,770
Anyway, thanks for looking out for us.

576
00:32:18,837 --> 00:32:21,773
Thank me later and get moving.

577
00:32:21,840 --> 00:32:24,109
What do you mean, get moving?

578
00:32:24,176 --> 00:32:26,711
Go load the cabbages.
You have an hour, right?

579
00:32:26,778 --> 00:32:28,013
Hurry up and move!

580
00:32:28,079 --> 00:32:29,614
-Move it!
-Okay, okay.

581
00:32:29,681 --> 00:32:31,583
-Hurry back.
-Yes, Boss! Off we go!

582
00:32:31,650 --> 00:32:33,885
Bring back lots of cabbages!

583
00:32:38,356 --> 00:32:40,992
MANURE COMPOST

584
00:32:42,661 --> 00:32:44,496
I'm seriously losing my mind.

585
00:32:45,230 --> 00:32:46,698
Oh, Su-yeon.

586
00:32:46,765 --> 00:32:49,067
How long do we have to stay like this?

587
00:32:49,668 --> 00:32:53,905
Jeez, doesn't that guy
ever use the bathroom?

588
00:32:53,972 --> 00:32:55,207
Darn it.

589
00:33:04,449 --> 00:33:06,017
Who goes there?

590
00:33:07,619 --> 00:33:10,222
I have come to claim your head.

591
00:33:12,991 --> 00:33:14,693
You reckless fool.

592
00:33:14,759 --> 00:33:16,695
Men, attack!

593
00:33:30,442 --> 00:33:32,210
Who are you?

594
00:33:33,645 --> 00:33:36,548
Who on earth are you?

595
00:33:40,919 --> 00:33:43,321
You sure groan an awful lot.

596
00:33:44,422 --> 00:33:46,191
I am Sang-deuk.

597
00:33:48,460 --> 00:33:51,796
I should've just become an actor.

598
00:33:53,298 --> 00:33:55,700
What a pathetic show he's putting on.

599
00:33:55,767 --> 00:33:57,702
This is so annoying.

600
00:33:57,769 --> 00:33:59,638
What should I try next?

601
00:33:59,704 --> 00:34:02,007
Iljimae? Hong Gil-dong?

602
00:34:04,976 --> 00:34:07,312
Now I've got some real leverage.

603
00:34:09,881 --> 00:34:12,717
Hello? Yes, Mi-yeong.

604
00:34:12,784 --> 00:34:15,253
Did the opening ceremony go well?

605
00:34:15,320 --> 00:34:18,857
What? He went missing again?

606
00:34:18,924 --> 00:34:21,493
Okay, got it. Just hang on a bit.

607
00:34:25,697 --> 00:34:27,966
He's leaving. Look, he's leaving.

608
00:34:28,033 --> 00:34:30,001
Do not come out.

609
00:34:30,602 --> 00:34:31,670
Huh? Oh, no.

610
00:34:31,736 --> 00:34:33,505
What? What is it?

611
00:34:34,105 --> 00:34:34,973
Where to?

612
00:34:35,040 --> 00:34:36,841
Something came up with Mi-yeong.

613
00:34:36,908 --> 00:34:39,244
Watch that today so no one steals it.

614
00:34:39,311 --> 00:34:40,845
-Okay, take care.
-Take care.

615
00:34:40,912 --> 00:34:41,780
MANURE COMPOST

616
00:34:41,846 --> 00:34:45,050
Is barbed wire a household item now?

617
00:34:47,686 --> 00:34:50,288
Ki-jun, that's enough. Come over here.

618
00:34:51,990 --> 00:34:53,758
You can handle this alone, right?

619
00:34:53,825 --> 00:34:56,661
Sure, they won't even dare steal them.

620
00:34:56,728 --> 00:34:58,597
Exactly. They're so precious to us.

621
00:34:58,663 --> 00:35:00,665
How dare they think of stealing them!

622
00:35:00,732 --> 00:35:04,603
All right, from now on,
it's 24-hour ironclad security!

623
00:35:04,669 --> 00:35:06,638
We're all taking shifts, okay?

624
00:35:06,705 --> 00:35:07,739
Right, in shifts.

625
00:35:07,806 --> 00:35:10,542
Go on for now. I'll keep watch.

626
00:35:11,142 --> 00:35:13,345
Gosh…

627
00:35:13,411 --> 00:35:16,281
This is driving me crazy, seriously.

628
00:35:22,787 --> 00:35:26,524
Once the cabbages are fully salted,
please put them on this shelf.

629
00:35:26,591 --> 00:35:27,792
So they salt evenly,

630
00:35:27,859 --> 00:35:30,228
don't forget to turn them regularly.

631
00:35:30,295 --> 00:35:31,696
Don't worry one bit.

632
00:35:31,763 --> 00:35:34,232
I'm an expert at salting cabbages.

633
00:35:34,299 --> 00:35:36,167
Thank you all so much.

634
00:35:36,234 --> 00:35:38,036
Sorry you're in the cold for us.

635
00:35:38,103 --> 00:35:42,173
Forget it. We have nothing to do,
so what's the point of sitting around?

636
00:35:42,240 --> 00:35:46,044
Once you make big money later,
treat us to black-bean noodles.

637
00:35:46,111 --> 00:35:47,779
Of course I will!

638
00:35:47,846 --> 00:35:49,948
Make mine a jumbo with extra noodles.

639
00:36:06,631 --> 00:36:08,600
What? Where are you heading again?

640
00:36:08,667 --> 00:36:11,670
Uh… I'm just running to the restroom.

641
00:36:11,736 --> 00:36:13,738
Oh, please. You're lying.

642
00:36:13,805 --> 00:36:16,875
You think I don't know
you're going to see In-ki?

643
00:36:17,509 --> 00:36:20,011
You catch on ridiculously fast. Jeez!

644
00:36:20,078 --> 00:36:21,880
Mom! Mom!

645
00:36:21,946 --> 00:36:26,117
I'm going crazy here.
She's totally swept up in romance.

646
00:36:26,751 --> 00:36:28,219
Just leave her alone, pal.

647
00:36:28,286 --> 00:36:31,990
They both like each other,
so what is wrong with them dating?

648
00:36:32,057 --> 00:36:34,826
What do you know?
Stop acting up and stay out, punk!

649
00:36:34,893 --> 00:36:37,529
-That is why you age fast, pal.
-Why, you jerk!

650
00:36:37,595 --> 00:36:40,832
Goodness, enough. Stop it, honestly.

651
00:36:40,899 --> 00:36:44,736
Keep it up, everyone,
and really pick up the pace!

652
00:36:48,339 --> 00:36:49,708
What are you staring at?

653
00:36:49,774 --> 00:36:52,510
There's a mountain of work. Get to it.

654
00:37:01,252 --> 00:37:03,555
Who dares block my path, scoundrel?

655
00:37:04,689 --> 00:37:07,358
I waited 18 years to avenge my master.

656
00:37:07,425 --> 00:37:11,196
I shall punish you with the sword art
taught to me by my master!

657
00:37:11,262 --> 00:37:14,999
Take this! Mantis Cabbage Fist!

658
00:37:19,370 --> 00:37:22,273
This isn't the Cabbage Fist I knew.

659
00:37:22,340 --> 00:37:26,111
This is my own creation,
Mantis Cabbage Fist of the North Star!

660
00:37:26,177 --> 00:37:27,746
In ten seconds, you will die.

661
00:37:27,812 --> 00:37:30,648
Then give my regards to my master.

662
00:37:35,353 --> 00:37:38,389
Wow! I should've been an actor.

663
00:37:38,456 --> 00:37:41,025
How has he been doing that all night?

664
00:37:41,092 --> 00:37:44,529
Those measly cabbages
aren't even worth much.

665
00:37:44,596 --> 00:37:46,931
There are way more down there.

666
00:37:46,998 --> 00:37:50,068
Ugh, what a bunch of idiots.

667
00:37:50,135 --> 00:37:52,737
-I'll go make a delivery first.
-I'll help you.

668
00:37:52,804 --> 00:37:56,141
I'm fine. Just do your own work.

669
00:37:56,207 --> 00:37:59,644
-Thanks, Yun-hui.
-Gosh, I told you I'm fine.

670
00:37:59,711 --> 00:38:03,148
Keep up the good work, everyone.
I'll go make the delivery.

671
00:38:03,214 --> 00:38:04,516
Be careful out there.

672
00:38:04,582 --> 00:38:06,217
Okay.

673
00:38:08,820 --> 00:38:11,322
YU-NA

674
00:38:14,359 --> 00:38:17,562
-Hey.
-Where are you going?

675
00:38:17,629 --> 00:38:20,165
I'm just getting some fresh air.

676
00:38:25,003 --> 00:38:27,672
-Hey, what's with you now?
-Where are you going?

677
00:38:27,739 --> 00:38:31,843
I'm going to relieve Ki-jun.
He's still guarding the cabbage field.

678
00:38:46,691 --> 00:38:48,359
Min-gi.

679
00:38:52,463 --> 00:38:55,333
Min-gi, talk to me.

680
00:38:55,400 --> 00:38:57,735
Do we have anything left to say?

681
00:38:57,802 --> 00:38:59,971
I'm sorry.

682
00:39:00,038 --> 00:39:01,906
I'm really sorry.

683
00:39:01,973 --> 00:39:04,042
Do you think saying sorry ends this?

684
00:39:04,108 --> 00:39:05,610
You deceived me.

685
00:39:05,677 --> 00:39:08,046
You knew Hyeok was blamed and hid it.

686
00:39:08,112 --> 00:39:09,514
And you used that too.

687
00:39:11,049 --> 00:39:13,318
Do you know what infuriates me most?

688
00:39:13,384 --> 00:39:16,054
The feelings I had for you all along

689
00:39:16,588 --> 00:39:18,423
have turned into nothing.

690
00:39:21,459 --> 00:39:22,327
I'm sorry.

691
00:39:22,393 --> 00:39:24,329
Why are you sorry?

692
00:39:24,395 --> 00:39:26,297
To you, I

693
00:39:26,364 --> 00:39:28,166
meant nothing at all.

694
00:39:28,233 --> 00:39:31,536
Did you do it just to toss me
an album like charity?

695
00:39:32,237 --> 00:39:34,806
How much of a fool
did you plan to make of me?

696
00:39:34,873 --> 00:39:37,141
How long would you
make me more miserable?

697
00:39:37,208 --> 00:39:39,010
-That's not it.
-Then what is it?

698
00:39:39,077 --> 00:39:40,645
I was scared.

699
00:39:41,546 --> 00:39:45,416
I was scared you'd go to Yun-hui.

700
00:39:45,483 --> 00:39:46,885
What do you mean by that?

701
00:39:46,951 --> 00:39:49,153
Your eyes used to look only at me.

702
00:39:49,220 --> 00:39:51,055
Seeing them turn to Yun-hui hurt.

703
00:39:51,122 --> 00:39:53,224
You used to think only of me.

704
00:39:53,291 --> 00:39:55,760
I got angry every time
you cared about Yun-hui.

705
00:39:55,827 --> 00:39:57,762
So no matter what it took…

706
00:39:57,829 --> 00:40:00,265
I wanted to keep you by my side.

707
00:40:00,331 --> 00:40:01,199
That's why.

708
00:40:01,266 --> 00:40:03,668
-It wasn't like that.
-You say it was pity?

709
00:40:03,735 --> 00:40:06,037
Or sympathy?

710
00:40:07,572 --> 00:40:11,342
No, it wasn't.

711
00:40:11,409 --> 00:40:13,945
If it were, I wouldn't have done this.

712
00:40:15,847 --> 00:40:18,416
Even though it's all pointless now,

713
00:40:18,483 --> 00:40:21,152
I wanted to be honest before I leave.

714
00:40:21,219 --> 00:40:23,121
You're leaving?

715
00:40:23,187 --> 00:40:24,822
I'm leaving…

716
00:40:26,224 --> 00:40:27,859
for the United States soon.

717
00:40:28,493 --> 00:40:30,895
I'm going to start from scratch there.

718
00:40:31,663 --> 00:40:34,599
This time, I'll live proudly on my own.

719
00:40:37,435 --> 00:40:39,304
I'll get going now.

720
00:40:40,071 --> 00:40:42,640
Thank you so much for everything,

721
00:40:44,042 --> 00:40:45,710
and I'm sorry.

722
00:40:49,347 --> 00:40:51,082
Take care, Min-gi.

723
00:41:39,597 --> 00:41:42,567
Hey, what are you doing here?

724
00:41:44,202 --> 00:41:45,737
Nothing much.

725
00:41:47,472 --> 00:41:50,308
Why? Is something on your mind?

726
00:41:51,142 --> 00:41:53,511
Are you like this because of Yu-na?

727
00:41:57,582 --> 00:42:00,284
I heard about it, more or less.

728
00:42:01,452 --> 00:42:03,287
She says she's leaving soon.

729
00:42:04,722 --> 00:42:05,656
Going abroad.

730
00:42:05,723 --> 00:42:07,492
Why so suddenly?

731
00:42:08,159 --> 00:42:10,094
She says she wants a fresh start.

732
00:42:14,899 --> 00:42:17,602
I never wanted to see her again.

733
00:42:18,970 --> 00:42:21,572
But now that she says she's leaving…

734
00:42:21,639 --> 00:42:24,342
I feel sad and sorry for her,

735
00:42:25,076 --> 00:42:26,544
I guess.

736
00:42:26,611 --> 00:42:30,548
Even though she left my head
in a mess right until the end.

737
00:42:31,449 --> 00:42:33,785
She left your head in a mess?

738
00:42:41,692 --> 00:42:43,728
Yun-hui.

739
00:42:43,795 --> 00:42:45,163
Yes? What is it?

740
00:42:52,937 --> 00:42:55,173
No, it's nothing.

741
00:42:59,043 --> 00:43:01,112
Let me lean on your shoulder.

742
00:43:04,182 --> 00:43:06,484
What's with you all of a sudden?

743
00:43:07,985 --> 00:43:09,987
Let's stay like this for a bit.

744
00:43:12,423 --> 00:43:14,525
Just a little longer…

745
00:43:18,529 --> 00:43:21,866
I am looking at you

746
00:43:21,933 --> 00:43:25,403
I am waiting only for you

747
00:43:25,470 --> 00:43:28,539
Always in the same spot

748
00:43:28,606 --> 00:43:31,476
In the same place

749
00:43:32,443 --> 00:43:35,913
Even when I miss you like crazy

750
00:43:35,980 --> 00:43:39,450
Even when I long for you like crazy

751
00:43:39,517 --> 00:43:42,587
Only my heart is crying

752
00:43:42,653 --> 00:43:44,489
What can I do?

753
00:43:55,099 --> 00:43:59,237
If you lay a hand on Lady Su-yeon,
you shall have to slay me first.

754
00:44:03,975 --> 00:44:05,643
Take that!

755
00:44:09,547 --> 00:44:11,315
Pathetic wretches.

756
00:44:12,617 --> 00:44:15,319
My lady, Lady Su-yeon!

757
00:44:16,654 --> 00:44:20,024
Young Master, I fear I won't make it.

758
00:44:20,091 --> 00:44:22,460
Please kiss me, Young Master.

759
00:44:23,661 --> 00:44:24,896
My lady.

760
00:44:24,962 --> 00:44:27,532
My lady, your face
has already grown so cold.

761
00:44:28,132 --> 00:44:30,902
Very well, I shall kiss you.

762
00:44:40,444 --> 00:44:42,513
Awesome!

763
00:44:42,580 --> 00:44:44,916
I should've been an actor, huh?

764
00:44:46,717 --> 00:44:48,319
Why should he be an actor?

765
00:44:48,386 --> 00:44:50,721
Is no one in this town normal?

766
00:44:50,788 --> 00:44:51,822
Nobody.

767
00:44:51,889 --> 00:44:55,660
You saw it. Every single one is weird,
every single one.

768
00:44:55,726 --> 00:45:00,064
But isn't Han-cheol kind of cute?

769
00:45:00,131 --> 00:45:02,200
What?

770
00:45:02,266 --> 00:45:06,904
Is this contagious?
She's turned into a nutjob too.

771
00:45:06,971 --> 00:45:10,007
Snap out of it, Su-yeon.

772
00:45:17,281 --> 00:45:19,450
Mom, could I have some more rice?

773
00:45:19,517 --> 00:45:21,819
You shameless punk, huh?

774
00:45:21,886 --> 00:45:25,223
You left without a word
and came back with some thick skin.

775
00:45:25,289 --> 00:45:27,992
I already said I was sorry, didn't I?

776
00:45:28,059 --> 00:45:29,927
Your appetite sure grew too.

777
00:45:29,994 --> 00:45:31,862
Give it here. I'll get you more.

778
00:45:31,929 --> 00:45:33,497
Thank you.

779
00:45:45,710 --> 00:45:47,345
What are you doing?

780
00:45:47,979 --> 00:45:48,980
Let me have this.

781
00:45:49,046 --> 00:45:50,448
You let me have it all.

782
00:45:51,148 --> 00:45:52,783
What are you talking about?

783
00:45:52,850 --> 00:45:55,586
This rolled omelet's mine,
and the rest is mine.

784
00:45:55,653 --> 00:45:56,687
Just deal with it.

785
00:45:56,754 --> 00:45:59,223
Your brain gets worse by the day…

786
00:45:59,290 --> 00:46:01,492
Isn't that right, Yun-hui?

787
00:46:01,559 --> 00:46:03,861
Gosh, stop it, you two, and eat this.

788
00:46:03,928 --> 00:46:06,063
You can have mine.

789
00:46:11,068 --> 00:46:12,703
Thanks.

790
00:46:13,304 --> 00:46:15,206
Hurry, hurry up and eat, everyone.

791
00:46:15,273 --> 00:46:17,675
I have to go
for the village hall remodeling.

792
00:46:17,742 --> 00:46:20,011
Village hall remodeling? What's that?

793
00:46:20,077 --> 00:46:23,314
For the elderly,
the Ministry of Rural Affairs and Food

794
00:46:23,381 --> 00:46:24,882
renovates the village hall

795
00:46:24,949 --> 00:46:26,784
and provides meals and all that.

796
00:46:27,718 --> 00:46:29,120
The government does that?

797
00:46:29,186 --> 00:46:32,256
Look, I'm busy,
so hurry, hurry up and eat.

798
00:46:42,266 --> 00:46:44,435
It's cold, so cold, darn it.

799
00:46:51,409 --> 00:46:53,277
He's relentless, truly relentless.

800
00:46:53,811 --> 00:46:56,514
He won't give us a chance to dig,
not one chance.

801
00:46:57,381 --> 00:46:58,783
Deck him and get the cash?

802
00:46:58,849 --> 00:47:01,986
We knock him out and go get the money.

803
00:47:02,053 --> 00:47:05,923
The three of us
can easily take him down, right?

804
00:47:05,990 --> 00:47:08,959
-No, we can't.
-Why not?

805
00:47:09,026 --> 00:47:12,596
Are you worried about that nutjob?

806
00:47:13,130 --> 00:47:14,899
No, uh… it's not that.

807
00:47:14,965 --> 00:47:18,202
I'm just worried others will catch us.

808
00:47:18,269 --> 00:47:21,472
But we can't stay like this forever.

809
00:47:21,539 --> 00:47:22,740
Let's go, hurry!

810
00:47:22,807 --> 00:47:24,275
-Hey!
-Agh!

811
00:47:24,342 --> 00:47:26,210
Hey! Jeez!

812
00:47:26,277 --> 00:47:30,548
Why did he show up again?
This is driving me crazy.

813
00:47:31,182 --> 00:47:35,453
Why can't I make a single putt lately?

814
00:47:35,519 --> 00:47:38,522
I'm losing all my money
because of this, all of it.

815
00:47:39,990 --> 00:47:41,826
ASSEMBLYMAN KIM BONG-NAM

816
00:47:41,892 --> 00:47:43,961
You made me shank it, you punk!

817
00:47:44,028 --> 00:47:46,297
-I apologize, sir.
-What is it?

818
00:47:47,531 --> 00:47:48,966
Did you find that guy?

819
00:47:49,033 --> 00:47:51,836
Not yet, but we located
that hostess bar girl.

820
00:47:51,902 --> 00:47:53,404
Really? Where is she?

821
00:47:56,474 --> 00:47:59,243
Here in Hadurong-ri, where
the meteorite was found,

822
00:48:00,010 --> 00:48:01,846
crowds are looking for more.

823
00:48:01,912 --> 00:48:04,382
What's this? A meteorite?

824
00:48:04,448 --> 00:48:05,316
What is this?

825
00:48:05,383 --> 00:48:07,084
Look closely, sir.

826
00:48:10,354 --> 00:48:13,691
So she's been hiding here.

827
00:48:15,593 --> 00:48:17,862
That should be enough. Let's go.

828
00:48:17,928 --> 00:48:19,563
Hyeok, you're on night watch?

829
00:48:19,630 --> 00:48:21,365
-Right.
-Hey, forget it!

830
00:48:21,432 --> 00:48:22,867
I stayed out all night.

831
00:48:22,933 --> 00:48:24,735
Not a soul in sight, not one.

832
00:48:24,802 --> 00:48:27,605
-Come on, let's go.
-Hey, guys!

833
00:48:30,274 --> 00:48:33,144
-What brings you here?
-The band is back together.

834
00:48:33,210 --> 00:48:34,945
We need a music video sequel!

835
00:48:35,012 --> 00:48:36,947
You're bringing that up again?

836
00:48:37,014 --> 00:48:39,283
The last one got three views. Three!

837
00:48:39,350 --> 00:48:42,319
That's because the video was crappy.

838
00:48:42,386 --> 00:48:45,289
So I even borrowed a camcorder.

839
00:48:45,356 --> 00:48:47,124
Let's film it properly this time.

840
00:48:47,191 --> 00:48:49,193
No, we can't. We're busy.

841
00:48:49,260 --> 00:48:51,829
Guys, this is the last time, please?

842
00:48:51,896 --> 00:48:53,130
It's the last time.

843
00:48:53,197 --> 00:48:54,999
Just this once, please?

844
00:48:55,933 --> 00:48:57,568
Oh, seriously.

845
00:49:02,807 --> 00:49:03,674
Huh?

846
00:49:03,741 --> 00:49:07,244
Do we really have to do this?

847
00:49:07,311 --> 00:49:09,246
Just do it. It's the last time.

848
00:49:09,313 --> 00:49:12,883
They're pulling every ridiculous stunt.

849
00:49:12,950 --> 00:49:14,151
Aren't you ready yet?

850
00:49:14,218 --> 00:49:17,188
Forget it, I can't wait any longer.

851
00:49:17,254 --> 00:49:20,191
Uh, mister, where are you going?

852
00:49:25,763 --> 00:49:27,031
What are you doing now?

853
00:49:27,097 --> 00:49:30,801
You two just keep quiet and watch.

854
00:49:40,444 --> 00:49:42,346
Hey, we're ready. Can we start?

855
00:49:42,947 --> 00:49:44,548
Okay, I'm ready.

856
00:49:44,615 --> 00:49:47,184
Min-gi, let's say hello and start.

857
00:49:47,251 --> 00:49:50,254
Hello! We're Modern Farmer! What!

858
00:49:50,321 --> 00:49:51,722
We will now begin singing.

859
00:49:51,789 --> 00:49:53,424
Here I go.

860
00:50:08,272 --> 00:50:11,308
Tear it all up without holding back

861
00:50:11,375 --> 00:50:14,912
Push on through with some grit

862
00:50:14,979 --> 00:50:18,582
Negative words, looks, harsh words

863
00:50:18,649 --> 00:50:21,018
Clear them out with some grit

864
00:50:21,919 --> 00:50:25,389
Even if they point and call me a fool

865
00:50:25,456 --> 00:50:29,159
Even if they scorn me as a nutjob

866
00:50:29,226 --> 00:50:32,530
Unlike phonies acting rich and smart

867
00:50:32,596 --> 00:50:35,065
I've got guts on a whole other level

868
00:50:35,132 --> 00:50:38,969
I'll keep flooring it, so watch me

869
00:50:41,839 --> 00:50:46,176
I'll pull it off my way, so watch me

870
00:50:48,412 --> 00:50:49,713
Freeze!

871
00:50:49,780 --> 00:50:51,315
Ah!

872
00:50:51,382 --> 00:50:52,883
A gun! A gun!

873
00:50:52,950 --> 00:50:54,752
Uh, why are you doing this, sir?

874
00:50:54,818 --> 00:50:57,621
-Shut up and put your hands up!
-My hands?

875
00:51:01,859 --> 00:51:04,395
Uh, Su-yeon, why are you here?

876
00:51:04,461 --> 00:51:06,030
There's no need for this.

877
00:51:06,096 --> 00:51:08,365
Then how long are we supposed to wait?

878
00:51:08,432 --> 00:51:12,970
Right, Su-yeon.
Let's find it fast and clear out.

879
00:51:14,905 --> 00:51:17,641
Isn't that the guy
who was stealing our cabbages?

880
00:51:17,708 --> 00:51:18,642
You're right.

881
00:51:18,709 --> 00:51:21,845
Why use a gun just to steal cabbages?

882
00:51:21,912 --> 00:51:23,981
Shut up! Clear out all these cabbages!

883
00:51:24,048 --> 00:51:26,483
Mister, no, Big Bro!

884
00:51:26,550 --> 00:51:28,852
These cabbages are our life savings.

885
00:51:28,919 --> 00:51:31,121
And they're barely worth anything.

886
00:51:31,188 --> 00:51:33,290
Who said I'm taking your cabbages?

887
00:51:33,357 --> 00:51:35,926
Clear them all out now, or I'll shoot!

888
00:51:35,993 --> 00:51:37,695
Ah! Why!

889
00:51:39,530 --> 00:51:41,532
-Faster!
-Faster! Faster!

890
00:51:41,599 --> 00:51:42,900
Faster!

891
00:51:42,967 --> 00:51:44,602
Why are you even doing this?

892
00:51:48,839 --> 00:51:51,609
Jeez! The ground is frozen.
We can't dig any deeper!

893
00:51:51,675 --> 00:51:52,876
I said dig, so dig!

894
00:51:52,943 --> 00:51:54,745
Yes, sir.

895
00:51:58,682 --> 00:51:59,984
It's because of this.

896
00:52:00,517 --> 00:52:02,720
-What is this?
-I don't know!

897
00:52:05,422 --> 00:52:07,358
Money, money, money.

898
00:52:07,424 --> 00:52:09,994
-How much is all this?
-Why is this here?

899
00:52:10,060 --> 00:52:11,161
Keep quiet.

900
00:52:11,228 --> 00:52:12,563
Bring the money here.

901
00:52:12,630 --> 00:52:14,765
-Hurry up!
-Yes, okay.

902
00:52:19,136 --> 00:52:20,738
You two, keep digging!

903
00:52:20,804 --> 00:52:23,207
I'll shoot!

904
00:52:25,709 --> 00:52:27,544
This is the last of it.

905
00:52:27,611 --> 00:52:29,246
There's nothing left.

906
00:52:31,548 --> 00:52:32,616
We finally found it!

907
00:52:32,683 --> 00:52:34,184
Finally.

908
00:52:35,352 --> 00:52:38,622
Su-yeon, we're rich now!

909
00:52:38,689 --> 00:52:40,524
Rich!

910
00:52:41,158 --> 00:52:42,626
What's with you two?

911
00:52:42,693 --> 00:52:44,328
Hey, get over there too!

912
00:52:44,395 --> 00:52:47,498
Hey, what are you doing right now?

913
00:52:47,998 --> 00:52:49,366
That wasn't the deal!

914
00:52:49,433 --> 00:52:50,934
This isn't just any money!

915
00:52:51,001 --> 00:52:53,070
I risked my life to steal this money!

916
00:52:53,137 --> 00:52:55,839
You think I'd share this with you two?

917
00:52:55,906 --> 00:52:57,975
-Ugh, you cheap jerk!
-I'll shoot!

918
00:52:58,742 --> 00:53:02,012
If you don't want to get hurt,
hands up and get over there.

919
00:53:02,513 --> 00:53:03,614
Back off, jeez.

920
00:53:10,854 --> 00:53:13,924
I did it. It's all done!

921
00:53:15,192 --> 00:53:18,295
Well, fancy meeting you here.

922
00:53:22,399 --> 00:53:24,635
You… How did you get here?

923
00:53:25,536 --> 00:53:30,441
You thought you could escape me, huh?

924
00:53:31,241 --> 00:53:34,978
You dare touch my money? You idiot!

925
00:53:35,045 --> 00:53:37,715
If you'd spared my life,
I'd never have done this.

926
00:53:37,781 --> 00:53:41,919
You made me do all the dirty work
while you lived the high life alone!

927
00:53:41,985 --> 00:53:43,554
Ha!

928
00:53:43,620 --> 00:53:48,092
Because that's all you're good for.

929
00:53:48,158 --> 00:53:51,228
Someone to use for dirty work
and toss when not needed.

930
00:53:51,295 --> 00:53:52,730
Nothing more than that.

931
00:53:52,796 --> 00:53:54,832
Shut up! Before I shoot you!

932
00:53:58,268 --> 00:54:00,270
Go ahead and shoot.

933
00:54:00,337 --> 00:54:01,772
You think I won't shoot?

934
00:54:01,839 --> 00:54:03,640
Pull the trigger, you bastard.

935
00:54:08,712 --> 00:54:10,547
This isn't real.

936
00:54:12,216 --> 00:54:14,284
You thought a toy would fool me?

937
00:54:14,351 --> 00:54:15,686
You dare mess with me!

938
00:54:17,187 --> 00:54:19,423
I got spooked for nothing.

939
00:54:21,525 --> 00:54:24,394
What are you doing, punk?
Go on and load up the money.

940
00:54:24,461 --> 00:54:27,264
Assemblyman, what do we do
with all these things?

941
00:54:27,331 --> 00:54:28,699
What do you think we do?

942
00:54:28,766 --> 00:54:31,735
You have no sense for how things work.

943
00:54:31,802 --> 00:54:34,104
We have to dispose of them all.

944
00:54:52,589 --> 00:54:57,728
Now I can finally sleep easy.

945
00:55:15,379 --> 00:55:17,548
What is this? What is it this time?

946
00:55:24,321 --> 00:55:25,656
Get out of the way.

947
00:55:25,722 --> 00:55:29,493
Hey, back off!
Tractors come first on farm roads!

948
00:55:29,560 --> 00:55:32,396
Do cars come first?
When this rig comes through,

949
00:55:32,462 --> 00:55:33,864
you ought to pull over!

950
00:55:33,931 --> 00:55:35,999
Why is that car barging right in?

951
00:55:36,500 --> 00:55:38,268
Move that tiller, mister!

952
00:55:39,169 --> 00:55:41,238
No idea what you're talking about.

953
00:55:50,314 --> 00:55:51,949
I said to move it, sir.

954
00:55:52,015 --> 00:55:53,116
What do you mean?

955
00:55:55,819 --> 00:55:57,087
Jeez, I said move it!

956
00:55:57,154 --> 00:55:59,189
Hey, get your hand off me!

957
00:55:59,256 --> 00:56:01,725
Hey, I was trying to live quietly.

958
00:56:01,792 --> 00:56:04,361
Man-gu's causing real trouble today!

959
00:56:04,428 --> 00:56:06,096
Why, you bastard!

960
00:56:32,022 --> 00:56:33,924
-Seriously?
-What is this now?

961
00:56:36,860 --> 00:56:38,629
Are you all right, Boss?

962
00:56:38,695 --> 00:56:40,530
I apologize. I'll handle it now.

963
00:56:40,597 --> 00:56:42,833
Darn it.

964
00:56:49,940 --> 00:56:51,508
Hey, you.

965
00:56:52,309 --> 00:56:54,444
-Hey! Darn it!
-Ow!

966
00:56:54,511 --> 00:56:57,114
I want to marry Mi-yeong.

967
00:56:58,615 --> 00:56:59,483
Who are you?

968
00:56:59,549 --> 00:57:01,184
What are you doing in the road?

969
00:57:01,251 --> 00:57:02,686
Get out of the way, punk!

970
00:57:02,753 --> 00:57:04,388
What, "punk"?

971
00:57:04,454 --> 00:57:06,156
You're no older than my nephew!

972
00:57:06,223 --> 00:57:08,158
How dare you talk down to me?

973
00:57:08,759 --> 00:57:10,427
Does this town have bad energy?

974
00:57:10,494 --> 00:57:12,429
Why are there so many lunatics?

975
00:57:12,496 --> 00:57:14,665
Hey, get up. Get up.

976
00:57:17,067 --> 00:57:18,135
Get out of the way.

977
00:57:18,201 --> 00:57:19,770
Get out of the way, you punk!

978
00:57:20,404 --> 00:57:22,806
I was trying to turn over a new leaf.

979
00:57:22,873 --> 00:57:24,975
Chang-deuk's causing trouble again!

980
00:57:26,543 --> 00:57:28,078
This punk.

981
00:57:41,091 --> 00:57:42,793
Why are you making extra work?

982
00:57:42,859 --> 00:57:43,827
Clear him away.

983
00:57:43,894 --> 00:57:45,963
What a psycho bastard.

984
00:57:47,965 --> 00:57:49,933
Take your hands off my grandson.

985
00:57:51,435 --> 00:57:54,004
What's with this old man now?

986
00:57:54,071 --> 00:57:55,973
Old man, go on your way over there.

987
00:57:56,039 --> 00:57:58,008
Please go. Just leave.

988
00:57:58,075 --> 00:57:59,109
My candy bar!

989
00:57:59,176 --> 00:58:00,510
How dare this little…

990
00:58:00,577 --> 00:58:04,681
I see this guy hasn't heard
any of the rumors about me.

991
00:58:04,748 --> 00:58:06,883
What, what? What are you, old man?

992
00:58:06,950 --> 00:58:09,052
Ek, ek!

993
00:58:14,925 --> 00:58:16,393
You old man!

994
00:58:34,144 --> 00:58:35,545
Grandpa!

995
00:58:35,612 --> 00:58:38,015
Would you look at that.

996
00:58:38,081 --> 00:58:40,050
Grandpa! Grandpa!

997
00:58:40,117 --> 00:58:42,019
I almost died. Thank you so much.

998
00:58:42,085 --> 00:58:43,153
You evil bastard!

999
00:58:43,220 --> 00:58:46,490
Thank you so much! We almost died.

1000
00:58:46,556 --> 00:58:49,459
We nearly died out here, Grandpa!

1001
00:58:54,898 --> 00:58:57,634
You punk, I'm Kim Seong-ju!

1002
00:58:57,701 --> 00:58:58,869
Lawmaker Kim Seong-ju!

1003
00:58:59,836 --> 00:59:01,438
Heard of immunity from arrest?

1004
00:59:01,505 --> 00:59:03,840
I have nothing to do with this. Check!

1005
00:59:03,907 --> 00:59:06,376
Let's go talk at the police station.

1006
00:59:06,443 --> 00:59:09,212
Station? The station?
Who's your police chief, punk?

1007
00:59:09,279 --> 00:59:10,947
Get in, get in, get in!

1008
00:59:11,014 --> 00:59:13,283
We'll talk there. Hurry and get in!

1009
00:59:26,863 --> 00:59:29,132
Those rotten, corrupt bastards.

1010
00:59:29,199 --> 00:59:33,236
With lawmakers like him, no wonder
the country's in such a sorry state.

1011
00:59:33,303 --> 00:59:34,371
Tell me about it.

1012
00:59:34,438 --> 00:59:36,540
Serves you right, you bastards!

1013
00:59:36,606 --> 00:59:37,774
Thanks so much, sir.

1014
00:59:37,841 --> 00:59:39,309
You saved me. Thank you.

1015
00:59:39,376 --> 00:59:41,278
It was nothing, really.

1016
00:59:41,344 --> 00:59:43,780
How can I ever repay you?

1017
00:59:43,847 --> 00:59:45,582
Oh, right! My camcorder!

1018
00:59:45,649 --> 00:59:48,351
I borrowed it. I can't lose it, shoot.

1019
00:59:51,354 --> 00:59:53,156
When will we get to Hadu-ri?

1020
00:59:53,223 --> 00:59:54,324
This is rough.

1021
00:59:56,893 --> 01:00:00,597
Lee Su-yeon, what's going on?

1022
01:00:00,664 --> 01:00:03,567
Tell me what on earth is going on.

1023
01:00:03,633 --> 01:00:05,469
Well, that's…

1024
01:00:05,535 --> 01:00:07,704
Han-cheol, it's just…

1025
01:00:07,771 --> 01:00:09,639
I mean…

1026
01:00:13,777 --> 01:00:15,345
Su-yeon.

1027
01:00:16,279 --> 01:00:19,950
So all this time… you were over there

1028
01:00:20,016 --> 01:00:23,220
looking for that money, is that it?

1029
01:00:29,693 --> 01:00:33,130
You weren't stealing sweet potatoes,

1030
01:00:35,065 --> 01:00:37,334
and you're not a college volunteer?

1031
01:00:45,208 --> 01:00:47,377
How could you do this to me?

1032
01:00:47,444 --> 01:00:51,114
Where do your lies begin and end?

1033
01:00:51,181 --> 01:00:53,150
Then the Su-yeon I knew…

1034
01:00:54,985 --> 01:00:56,586
no, wait, then…

1035
01:00:57,888 --> 01:00:59,923
the side of you that I loved…

1036
01:01:01,725 --> 01:01:04,594
that wasn't a lie, right? Right?

1037
01:01:06,796 --> 01:01:08,865
I'm sorry.

1038
01:01:08,932 --> 01:01:12,269
I'm so sorry.

1039
01:01:20,677 --> 01:01:22,445
Does being sorry fix everything?

1040
01:01:22,512 --> 01:01:25,849
You toyed with my heart for money,

1041
01:01:25,916 --> 01:01:27,317
and "sorry" ends it all?

1042
01:01:27,384 --> 01:01:29,920
I never played with your feelings.

1043
01:01:29,986 --> 01:01:33,623
My feelings for you were real.

1044
01:01:34,724 --> 01:01:36,493
Stop it.

1045
01:01:36,993 --> 01:01:39,629
I can't believe anything anymore!

1046
01:01:43,400 --> 01:01:46,002
All right, I lied.

1047
01:01:46,069 --> 01:01:49,139
But I wanted to find that money
and study abroad too.

1048
01:01:50,140 --> 01:01:52,976
I wanted to shed the stigma of my past

1049
01:01:53,043 --> 01:01:56,379
and stop pouring drinks for men
just to make a living.

1050
01:01:56,980 --> 01:01:59,749
Was that really so wrong of me?

1051
01:02:01,218 --> 01:02:04,087
Is that really so wrong?

1052
01:02:12,562 --> 01:02:13,563
Han-cheol!

1053
01:02:13,630 --> 01:02:15,098
Han-cheol, what's wrong?

1054
01:02:15,165 --> 01:02:16,066
Han-cheol!

1055
01:02:16,132 --> 01:02:17,734
Han-cheol!

1056
01:02:18,635 --> 01:02:19,603
Han-cheol!

1057
01:02:19,669 --> 01:02:21,605
Han-cheol! Han-cheol!
